<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goh Chok Tong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goh Chok Tong (born 1941) is a Singaporean politician who served as the second prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> from 1990 to 2004, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew">Lee Kuan Yew</a>. A former shipping executive, he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-action-party">People's Action Party</a> government through strong growth, the Asian financial crisis of 1997 and the SARS outbreak of 2003, and promoted a more consultative style of rule. He later served as senior minister.</p></div>
